    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d4">

                <pb facs="0019" n="5" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg5"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Conference W And PW/1–1245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San Jose</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-01-12T13:00:00-06:00">January 12, 1945—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>34. Reference Department’s circular January 11, 7 p.m. Costa Rican Foreign
                        Minister<anchor n="5" xml:id="d4-f1"/> has informed me that he is in
                    complete accord with the agenda outlined in Department’s circular of January
                    5.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d4-f1" n="5" xml:id="d4-f1-content">
                <p>Julio Acosta García.</p>
